 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "The Sao were organised in small kingdoms or city-states, each with walled towns ruled by a chief. They believed in spirits and ancestors, and buried their dead in large jars.\nDecline of the Sao: from about the 15th and 16th centuries they were conquered and absorbed by the Kanem-Bornu empire, and Islam spread in the region. Their descendants mixed with other peoples; the Kotoko are thought to be among them.\nThe Pygmies today: their forest is shrinking because of logging and farming; many have been encouraged to settle in villages along roads. They face problems of land rights, health and schooling, while trying to keep their culture and knowledge of the forest.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
